
Start();
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking;
search GroupFields Utilities list;

register(Utilities);
define
    haProbe code={
        haH := hasActioN;
        cerr "HA " taG " -> " haH:;
        };
    haRun code={
        haProbe(IF);
        haProbe(DO);
        haProbe(FOR);
        haProbe(ExpressioN);
        haProbe(NamE);
        haProbe(SemI);
        };
    ;
haRun();
cerr "HASACTION SENTINEL":;
stop();

hasActionT -- SEQ 205 R2 (Tony, 2026-10-06): hasActioN (opDot 36) answers from the rule's actor, "this rule has an
action", read here AT REST: nothing in this file fires IF, DO, FOR, ExpressioN or NamE before the read.

Before the actionMethod retirement it read the RuleStuff.actionMethod cache, which only the isCoded arm of setActions
filled at definition; every other rule's cache was filled by fireLabelMethod's lazy install at its first fire. So these
five read 0 at rest on trunk (born red) and 1 once the cache retires and the read asks builtinActoR.

SemI is the control: a grammar term with no actor reads 0 on both builds, so a read that answered 1 for everything
would fail it.

Each value is read inside haProbe on the rule handed in -- reading off a holder answers for the holder.
